      "last_updated": "2026-05-12T00:00:00.000000",
      "title_align": "left",
      "section": "Steps",
      "order": 6,
      "alignment": "left",
      "vertical_alignment": "top",
      "body": "Two synthetic samples, each registered in four steps as elastix or ANTs would do it: the raw moving image, then after a rigid, an affine and a B-spline transform. Pick a step in the viewer to see its output laid over the fixed image, with the step's metrics beside it. embryo_a improves at every step. embryo_b fails at the affine step: the shear is fitted the wrong way round, so it ends up further from the fixed image than after the rigid step, and the B-spline cannot fully recover and folds the image in one place. The plots draw both samples; the Sample filter narrows them and the viewer to one.\n",
      "surface": "none",
      "accent": null,
      "logo": null,
      "logo_dark": null,
      "wf_tag": "python/bioimage_demo"
    },
